IGA (Intel(R) Graphics Assembler) API headers - fetched at build time from public upstream.

Component:   IGA C API headers from intel-graphics-compiler (iga.h,
             iga_types_ext.hpp, iga_types_swsb.hpp, iga_bxml_ops.hpp,
             iga_bxml_enums.hpp)
Upstream:    https://github.com/intel/intel-graphics-compiler
Version:     pinned by IGA_COMMIT_ID in tools/unitrace/CMakeLists.txt, the single
             source of truth (not repeated here)
License:     MIT (see ./LICENSE: upstream's LICENSE.md notice, followed by the
             MIT License text it refers to)

How it is used: scripts/get_iga_headers.py clones intel-graphics-compiler at
IGA_COMMIT_ID and copies the IGA headers into the build tree; unitrace compiles
against them. The iga64 library itself is loaded at runtime from the system and
is not distributed with unitrace.

To bump: update IGA_COMMIT_ID, refresh LICENSE from upstream at the new commit,
and update tools/unitrace/third-party-programs.txt if the license or copyright
changed.
